{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Take away</b> — the songs of the Levites, and the word 'noise' refers to them, as if he said: take away the assembly of the Levites who sing. Or it is derived from <b>המית</b> ים (the silencing of songs)."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The phrase המית ים is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally as it appears in the source. The second או reading seems to derive המון from a root meaning 'to silence/cut off', with ים as an appended example word."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:12.830132349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}